roys value.","It converts 16% of revenue into free cash flow, or 8% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.60x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.0x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 12pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 10.4% of revenue on R&D and 7.7% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $5.5B (6% of market cap)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 27.7% over 3 years and 36.6% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","Free cash flow has compounded 71.6% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+4.1% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 38%.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (1.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 45, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (47 sales, net $23.6M sold)."],"people":["With about 31,400 employees, each generates about $437K of revenue, in line with the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 36.6% a year.","That works out to $69K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $432K (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $33K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":42,"head":"Avoid: priced 124% above its fair value of $80.15.","pros":["FCF margin 15.8%","Revenue grew 36.6%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $5.5B","Altman Z in the safe zone","40 analysts' mean target $251 (+40%)"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 23, gates 4/24)","Trades 124% above fair value of $80.15","ROIC 19.4% v